* Piezo harvester, linear: power into a resistive load at resonance, against the closed form.
*
* The cantilever of models/multiphysics/piezo/piezo_parts.va (10 g effective mass, 50 Hz,
* damping ratio 1 %, coupling 5e-4 N/V, piezo capacitance 50 nF), shaken at its 50 Hz resonance
* with 2 m/s^2 of base acceleration, into R = 1/(w Cp) = 63.66 kOhm.
*
* Closed form (the coupled two-degree-of-freedom steady state, Z = R || Cp):
*   X = -m a / (k - m w^2 + j w c + j w theta^2 Z),   V = j w theta X Z
*   |V| = 6.3193 V, |X| = 0.8937 mm, P = |V|^2 / 2R = 0.3136 mW.
* Measured (2.16.1+3, amplitude from the RMS over the last 10 cycles; see piezo_plots.py):
*   6.3194 V at this deck's 20 us step cap. The step matters here: a resonator with Q ~ 50
*   magnifies the trapezoidal rule's small frequency error (second order in the step), and a
*   0.1 ms cap reads 6.3241 V (+0.08 %), 0.05 ms 6.3206 V.
* Plot: python docs/examples/multiphysics/piezo_plots.py target/release/va-cli
* Run: va-cli sim circuits/multiphysics/piezo_linear.net --model models/multiphysics/piezo --tran --report p
VA acc gnd SIN(0 2 50)
X1 acc p gnd piezo_beam
R1 p gnd 63662
.tran 0.02m 3
.end
